From: Octagon SF8008 port
Subject: [PATCH] gfbdc: start drawing on the page that is displayed

setResolution() ends by swapping surface and surface_back, so rendering
starts on the second page of the framebuffer. That is only correct if
something afterwards pans the display to that page, but flip() is
issued from eWidgetDesktop::redrawComposition(), which returns straight
away unless the desktop runs in buffered composition mode. In the
immediate mode used for normal operation no flip is ever submitted, the
display keeps scanning out the first page and everything that is drawn
lands on a page that is never shown.

It also leaves the live drawing surface pointing at nothing when the
framebuffer provides a single page only, because the swap then installs
the null pointer that was just stored in surface_back, and the next
gPixmap::fill() dereferences address 0.

Drop the swap and keep rendering on the page the framebuffer starts on.
The flip handler swaps the two surfaces itself, so buffered composition
is unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Pending
--- a/lib/gdi/gfbdc.cpp
+++ b/lib/gdi/gfbdc.cpp
@@ -522,15 +522,6 @@
 	dreamGE2DRegisterFramebuffer(fb->lfb, base_phys, surface.x, surface.y, surface.stride, m_number_of_pages);
 #endif
 
-#if defined(CONFIG_HISILICON_FB)
-	if(islocked()==0)
-	{
-		gUnmanagedSurface s(surface);
-		surface = surface_back;
-		surface_back = s;
-	}
-#endif
-
 	m_pixmap = new gPixmap(&surface);
 	invalidateNativeSpinner();
 
